                                "sense_id": "7f3a6a72-7daa-3877-9a7b-78b9ae45fc53",
                                "text": "2001: The first successful drug of this class was omeprazole (sold under the trade name Losec®), and it helped to change the medium-sized Swedish pharmaceutical company Astra, which discovered it, into a major player in the pharmaceutical industry. — Leslie Iversen, Drugs: A Very Short Introduction (Oxford 2001, p. 46)"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
